'''John Wesley "Lam" Jones''' (April 4, 1958 – March 15, 2019) was an American athlete who won a [[gold medal]] in the [[4 × 100 meter relay]] at the [[1976 Summer Olympics]] in [[Montreal]] and played professional [[American football|football]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) as a [[wide receiver]] for the [[New York Jets]] and [[Dallas Cowboys]]. Prior to that, he played [[college football]] and ran track at the [[University of Texas]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2019-03-15 |title=Former Texas star, Olympian Johnny 'Lam' Jones passes away after cancer battle |url=https://www.hookem.com/2019/03/15/former-texas-star-olympian-johnny-lam-jones-passes-away-cancer-battle/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190323003644/https://www.hookem.com/2019/03/15/former-texas-star-olympian-johnny-lam-jones-passes-away-cancer-battle/ |archive-date=2019-03-23 |access-date=2025-10-15 |work=Hookem.com |language=en-US}}</ref>

